'''Calette''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that was introduced in [[Version 8.7 Update|Version 8.7]] and can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Princess Punt Sweets Collaboration Event]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 485
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Calette
|name2 = Calette CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Calette CC''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Realistically, this unit's usage is limited at best. The superior generalist value from readily attainable [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]] outshines her in many situations. However, it is worth noting that her recharge rate is noticeably shorter, giving her an edge in replaceability.

If her niche in and of itself were more powerful, then perhaps her usage would be realistically understandable. Many short-ranged Angel enemies are countered by either [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]'s unmatched spammability, or [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet the Maiko]]'s high range depending on what the situation calls for. The same applies to Aliens, where [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] is more expendable and can retain a near-100% uptime on Freeze if two are out on the field (which is not very difficult to achieve). Additionally, Talented [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] offers a another useful skillset with much less risk involved despite his Single Attack. Zombies are especially a lost cause, as she is almost entirely outperformed by [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], functioning as a diet version of Calette with a generally better ability, more stacking potential as both a DPS and support, as well as pierce. This isn't mentioning how Zombies can burrow into her relatively easily. There is merit to using Calette in mixed-trait stages featuring a plethora of the aforementioned traits, providing extra assurance from the safety of the backline. However, these cases are seldom, so treat her as a last line of defense if the going gets rough.

